# Tests

Two suites, split by Maven plugin:

- `*Test.java` — unit tests (Surefire). No Spring context. Construct the class under test and mock the layer directly beneath it with Mockito.
- `*IT.java` — integration tests (Failsafe). Extend `AbstractIT` (`@SpringBootTest` on a random port, profile `test`, REST Assured).

Name tests `should…`. Structure them with `//given`, `//when`, and `//then` comments. Assert the result and `verify` the collaborator. Reuse fixtures from `template.util.TestItems` instead of duplicating item builders.

```java
@Test
void shouldGetItem() {
    //given item
    var item = Item.builder().id(1L).name("Item A").build();
    //and service
    var service = mock(ItemService.class);
    when(service.get(1L)).thenReturn(Optional.of(item));
    //when item is requested
    var response = new ItemController(service, new ModelMapper()).getItem(1L);
    //then OK status is returned
    assertEquals(OK, response.getStatusCode());
    verify(service).get(1L);
}
```

Integration tests that insert data delete it before the method returns. Run `./mvnw clean verify` before considering a change done.
